<refnamediv>
  <refname><function>SilikoEvaluate</function></refname>
  <refpurpose>Function to evaluate a <type>SilikoNode</type> with a
    <type>SilikoEngine</type></refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<programlisting language="C">#include &lt;SilikoCore/Evaluate.h&gt;</programlisting>
<programlisting language="C">SilikoValue *SilikoEvaluate(
    SilikoEngine *engine,
    const SilikoNode *node);</programlisting>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
<title>Description</title>
<para>The <function>SilikoEvaluate</function> function evaluates
<varname>node</varname> using <varname>engine</varname> to resolve
operators and function calls.</para>
</refsection>

<refsection>
<title>Return Values</title>

<para>The <function>SilikoEvaluate</function> function returns the value
obtained by evaluating the tree. Error values will propagate based on
the rules within functions called during evaluation. Siliko Core’s
built-in functions normally return the first error they encounter when
evaluating from left to right.</para>
</refsection>
